      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T17:08:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From https://lore.kernel.org/all/a49619b7-2340-2726-8c7e-df6ff0c1793a@gmail.com/: \"Typically extensions to the core require at least one user. So you should\nadd your driver, that makes use of the changes, to the series.\nAnd best explain what\u0027s special with your hardware so that it needs a core\nextension whilst drivers for other hardware are fine with the core as-is.\"\n\nPlease follow the upstream-first policy.",
      "revId": "5c8fec5a0ff0ba43756d49aea4a6847bbe152d15",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b35cca57_700a0e9a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
